 573:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** /*
 574:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * Usually in Renode we want to skip DDR training, as it is slow and does not
 575:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * do anything useful. If the user wants to explicitly simulate the training,
 576:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * then RENODE_SIM_DDR_TRAINING should be defined.
 577:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * The Training skip is achieved by reading from a register that should always
 578:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * return 0's in Hardware. In this case, the MPFS_DDRMock module will return
 579:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * a known pattern that will let us know we are in a simulation, and will skip
 580:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * the training.
 581:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * The RPC_RESET_MAIN_PLL register can usually only return 0x00 or 0x01, as
 582:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * the other bits are set to Rreturns0. This signature string "REND" will only
 583:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  * ever be read when connected to the Renode MPFS_DDRMock module.
 584:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  */
 585:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** #ifndef RENODE_SIM_DDR_TRAINING
