4824:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****   The MSS_DDR_status() function is used to return status information to the
4825:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****   user.
4826:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** 
4827:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****   TODO: Define number of request inputs
4828:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** 
4829:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****    @param option
4830:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     This option chooses status data we wish returned
4831:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** 
4832:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****    @param return_data
4833:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     Returned data here. This must be within a defined range.
4834:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     todo:Detail on the sharing of data will be system dependent.
4835:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     AMP/SMU detail to be finalized at time of writing
4836:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** 
4837:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****   @return
4838:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     Returns 0 on success.
4839:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     TODO: Define error codes.
4840:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c **** 
4841:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****   Example:
4842:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     The call to MSS_DDR_status(DDR_TYPE, return_data) will return 0 if
4843:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     successful and the DDR type in the first four bytes of the ret_mem area.
4844:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     @code
4845:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     MSS_DDR_status( DDR_TYPE, ret_mem );
4846:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****     @endcode
4847:../src/platform/mpfs_hal/common/nwc/mss_ddr.c ****  */
